      "content": "#include <algorithm>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <utility>\n#include <vector>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\n\nint modPow(int value, int exponent) {\n    long long result = 1;\n    long long base = value;\n    while (exponent > 0) {\n        if (exponent & 1) result = result * base % MOD;\n        base = base * base % MOD;\n        exponent >>= 1;\n    }\n    return static_cast<int>(result);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n\n    int n, m;\n    cin >> n >> m;\n\n    vector<pair<int, int>> blocked;\n    blocked.reserve(m);\n    for (int i = 0; i < m; ++i) {\n        int row, col;\n        cin >> row >> col;\n        blocked.emplace_back(row, col);\n    }\n\n    sort(blocked.begin(), blocked.end());\n    blocked.erase(unique(blocked.begin(), blocked.end()), blocked.end());\n\n    if (binary_search(blocked.begin(), blocked.end(), make_pair(0, 0)) ||\n        binary_search(blocked.begin(), blocked.end(), make_pair(n - 1, n - 1))) {\n        cout << 0 << '\\n';\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    const int maxSteps = 2 * n - 2;\n    vector<int> factorial(maxSteps + 1), inverseFactorial(maxSteps + 1);\n    factorial[0] = 1;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= maxSteps; ++i) {\n        factorial[i] = static_cast<long long>(factorial[i - 1]) * i % MOD;\n    }\n    inverseFactorial[maxSteps] = modPow(factorial[maxSteps], MOD - 2);\n    for (int i = maxSteps; i > 0; --i) {\n        inverseFactorial[i - 1] = static_cast<long long>(inverseFactorial[i]) * i % MOD;\n    }\n\n    auto choose = [&](int total, int selected) -> int {\n        if (selected < 0 || selected > total) return 0;\n        return static_cast<long long>(factorial[total]) * inverseFactorial[selected] % MOD *\n               inverseFactorial[total - selected] % MOD;\n    };\n\n    vector<int> ways(blocked.size());\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < blocked.size(); ++i) {\n        const int row = blocked[i].first;\n        const int col = blocked[i].second;\n        long long count = choose(row + col, row);\n\n        for (size_t j = 0; j < i; ++j) {\n            const int previousRow = blocked[j].first;\n            const int previousCol = blocked[j].second;\n            if (previousCol <= col) {\n                const int rowDelta = row - previousRow;\n                const int colDelta = col - previousCol;\n                count -= static_cast<long long>(ways[j]) * choose(rowDelta + colDelta, rowDelta) % MOD;\n                if (count < 0) count += MOD;\n            }\n        }\n        ways[i] = static_cast<int>(count % MOD);\n    }\n\n    long long answer = choose(2 * n - 2, n - 1);\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < blocked.size(); ++i) {\n        const int row = blocked[i].first;\n        const int col = blocked[i].second;\n        if (row <= n - 1 && col <= n - 1) {\n            const int rowDelta = n - 1 - row;\n            const int colDelta = n - 1 - col;\n            answer -= static_cast<long long>(ways[i]) * choose(rowDelta + colDelta, rowDelta) % MOD;\n            if (answer < 0) answer += MOD;\n        }\n    }\n\n    cout << answer % MOD << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n",
      "path": "src/solution.cpp"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Representing blocked cells as a compact sorted list instead of an N-by-N bitmap removes the dominant quadratic memory footprint and improves locality for sparse inputs; combinatorial path subtraction computes the answer using that list without traversing the full grid.",
  "notes": "The obstacle-pair computation is O(K^2) for K distinct blocked cells, so its practical benefit depends on obstacle count. All arithmetic is modulo 1,000,000,007, and blocked start or destination cells return zero.",
  "sources_kept": [],
  "transformations": [
    "Replace the dense blocked-cell matrix and rolling-grid traversal with a compact sorted, deduplicated obstacle vector.",
    "Precompute factorials and inverse factorials, then count paths by subtracting paths through earlier dominating obstacles."
  ]
